{"clock":1,"nonce":"30ddfeacd0558cebcbefd00bdf3bc684","ops":[{"kind":"create","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792670541,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:5978899494"},"data":{"body":"The cycle protocol's M3 to M6 (docs/prd/cycle-protocol.md), after M1 and M2 landed with 7fd2891: the one page, the step bar, `[cycle]` criteria headings and kinds, the step buttons that move the status, each step's discussion, and Intent's criteria warnings.\n\n- **M3, step 3 with wtx:** Start opens the branch with `wtx go` in plan mode and a draft PR holding the plan; Revise goes through `wtx brief`; Approve takes the agent out of plan mode; `plans-in-pr` keeps plans out of PRs per project. Low risk starts the branch at step 4.\n- **M4, step 4, the tests and the checks:** `[cycle.tests.*]` suites and `[cycle.checks.*]`, proposed from lefthook, else the Makefile or package.json. git-board runs only the toml's argv; slow suites are CI's. Mark ready for review is gated on the server.\n- **M5, step 6, review:** the Changes view as the canvas's C6: threads sent to the agent, Approve and Request changes.\n- **M6, steps 2, 5 and 7:** C2's three risk options with the AI's suggestion; C5's commits and the PR's title and description; C7's checklist with who and when, and the run at the merged head.\n\nEach milestone gets its own branch. Out of scope: environments for e2e, reading CI results back, running CI locally, GB-21. The agent never decides pass or fail. Live checks go to guilbep/git-board-test or guilbep-sandbox only, never co2-calculator.\n\n\n- a normal-risk issue's Start opens a worktree and a draft PR with the plan, and Review unlocks when that PR is marked ready\n- the touched suites come pre-ticked, a fast suite runs in the worktree from the toml's argv, and a red check blocks Mark ready for review\n- a bug needs a test that fails before the fix, and a feature's criterion with no test is a warning\n- the page matches C6 at step 6\n- the pages match C2, C5 and C7\n- `make ci` and `cd web \u0026\u0026 npm run typecheck \u0026\u0026 npm test` pass for each milestone","title":"cycle: M3 to M6, plan with wtx, tests and checks, review, risk/code/verify screens"}},{"kind":"set-status","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792677719,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:5978899494"},"data":{"status":"closed"}},{"kind":"change-labels","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792679416,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:5978899494"},"data":{"add":["kind:feat","prio:p1","status:done","assignee:guilbep"],"remove":null}},{"kind":"comment","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792670542,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"comment:6340245655"},"data":{"body":"Built: C6's review screen (CycleReview.vue, from ChangesView.vue), the step 6 aside (ReviewAside.vue), Send to Claude Code on a thread (the thread quoted as data in the wtx prompt), Approve and Request changes. An approval needs its line now, like a change request.\n\nRulings\n- Approve and Request changes write a review at the head and move no status: no PRD rule moves it. The merge is what moves the issue on (Start verification, to the first validation status).\n- Structural risk needs 2 approvals, any other 1 (dev-cycle.md, \"a second human approval\").\n- The COMMENT verdict radio is gone: replies cover comments.\n\nDeferred\n- \"Against plan v2: k of n steps found\" in the sub-bar: no plan-vs-diff data yet.\n- The bot tag on the aside's rows: Person has no bot flag.\n\nNot checked live (scratch clone of guilbep/git-board-test, at 1440 and 900)\n- The PR link, checks and the PR's reviews in the sub-bar, and \"go to PR #N on GitHub\" in the aside: the clone's identity had no GitHub login or token in git-bug's keyring, so evidence.pr was empty. Unit tests cover checksLine and approvers.\n- Send to Claude Code against a real wtx: the fixture had no worktree. TestAgentBriefThread covers it.\n- Start verification on a merged PR: unit tests only.\n- After an Approve, the \"Someone else changed this issue\" notice showed once; it did not come back on a second try (Request changes). It looks like a race between the live event and the editor clearing. That logic dates from 624dfc2.\n\nFor the coordinator\n- make ci in the sandbox: everything passes except TestIssueSyncTakesTheAssigneesMode and TestForgeSyncSetsTheAssigneesMode, which fail the same way on main in the sandbox. Run make ci outside it before landing.\n- M3 overlap: internal/wtx/prompt.go gets Thread and a quote helper here, Then on M3's branch. Expect a small rebase.\n- Scratch left on guilbep/git-board-test: PR #29 and branch 57378c5-m5-review-live. Close and delete them, or keep them for a live check with a token."}},{"kind":"comment","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792670543,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"comment:6340245922"},"data":{"body":"**M3 handover** (branch b768fbb-m3-plan-with-wtx, HEAD e465feb)\n\n**What M3 does**\n- Start at step 3 (ready, normal risk, no plan) runs `wtx go \u003cbranch\u003e --prompt F --no-attach` with step 3's prompt. The prompt asks for the plan in plan mode, then, once it is accepted in the pane: commit it as `\u003cplans\u003e/\u003cissue\u003e-\u003cslug\u003e.md` with `issue:` and `status: draft` in its front matter, push, open a draft PR, and stop. The status stays ready. With `plans-in-pr = false` the prompt says no PR at this step.\n- Start work at low risk (or with the plan already approved) moves the status to in-progress and runs `wtx go` with step 4's prompt.\n- Approve posts `plan:approve`, moves the status to in-progress, then briefs the agent through `wtx brief` (only once a plan file exists; with no plan there is nothing to accept, and the server would refuse with no-plan).\n- Revise is the comment plus `wtx brief`, as before.\n- Step 3 shows the strip (worktree, agent state, draft PR link), the plan's meta (path, issue, status), and the approver's sentence. The draft PR shows on step 3's line and in the status bar. In-progress with a draft PR waits for it to be marked ready, and in-review with a draft PR offers no review.\n- The server adds no `git push` or `gh` surface. The agent pushes and opens the draft PR itself.\n\n**Not done: the live half of Done-when**\nChecked on a local scratch clone with a fake wtx: the go/brief argv, the prompts, the status moves, and the page at 1440px and 900px against C3/C4. Not checked:\n- A real `wtx go`: the sandbox refuses tmux (`error creating /private/tmp/tmux-502/...: Operation not permitted`).\n- The draft PR and `gh pr ready`: pointing the scratch clone at GitHub was denied. The strip's draft PR link has no test and no live run, so this check is its only coverage.\n\nTo check by hand, on a git-board-test clone with a `risk` field, serving this branch:\n1. A ready issue with criteria and normal risk. Press Start, then accept the plan in the agent's pane.\n2. The agent commits the plan, pushes, and opens the draft PR. The page should show the strip's draft link and \"draft PR #N\" on step 3's line (within the 5 minute PR cache).\n3. Approve. Accept again in the pane (see `--build` below). The agent writes and pushes the test.\n4. `gh pr ready N`. The \"Mark ready for review\" action appears, then Review at in-review.\n\n**Your call: wtx `brief --build`**\nNot made. The `buildBrief` constant in internal/server/worktrees.go stays false. `wtx brief` always restarts the pane in plan mode, so Approve and Revise restart the planner and the person accepts in the pane again. \"Approve takes the agent out of plan mode\" is therefore not delivered yet. The proposed wtx change, for a paired worktree of EPFL-ENAC/wtx:\n- cli.py: `brief --build`, and `cmd_brief` passes `phase=\"build\"`.\n- tmux.py:312: thread the phase through `ensure_session` instead of the hardcoded `\"plan\" if brief`.\n- `PLAN_INSTRUCTION` only for plan briefs. Effort `orch.build_effort`.\n- One test in wtx.\nThen flip `buildBrief` to true.\n\n**Rulings made here**\n- The draft note shows at step 5 only. At step 4 a draft PR is the step's own state (C4).\n- The approver's words: \"You approve\", else \"\u003clogin\u003e approves\", else \"The plan role approves\". The brief says \"approved by \u003clogin\u003e\" only when the approval has a login.\n\n**Deferred on purpose**\n- C3's plan versions (v1/v2, \"Changes since v1\", Edit): the plan's git history, worth its own item.\n- \"Open the session\" (nothing a browser can open), and parsing wtx's handoff record.\n- `plans-in-pr = false`: the plan stays on the branch, and the PR waits until step 5.\n- Structural risk at step 3 uses the same plan prompt. Structural plans normally go on a `plan/` branch PR.\n\n**Seen, not this branch's**\n- \"Approved by \" with an empty login: cycle.ts:91, CyclePlan.vue:29 (from M2).\n- \"Approve the plan\" and \"Ask the agent to revise\" are offered with no plan file. Approve with no plan now only moves the status, with no brief.\n- At 900px the header's \"Inbox\" and \"Send 1\" overlap.\n- On a scratch board, inbox follow answers 409 and environments 404.\n- `make ci` fails on TestIssueSyncTakesTheAssigneesMode (issuesync_test.go:92) and TestForgeSyncSetsTheAssigneesMode (assignable_test.go:152). Both fail on main locally too, and main's last three CI runs on GitHub are red (latest 39757059050). The branch doesn't touch those files. Web: typecheck clean, 163/163 tests.\n\n**For M4 to M6**\n- M4: step 4's prompt names the kind's rule. `[cycle.tests]` and `[cycle.checks]` slot in where the prompt's gate is built (worktrees.go, `cyc.Gate`).\n- M5: step 3 lives in CyclePlan.vue. IssueStep.vue only passes `agent` and handles `@approve` and the Start-work button.\n- M6: steps 2, 5 and 7 untouched."}},{"kind":"comment","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792677712,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"comment:6342661113"},"data":{"body":"M3 (step 3 with wtx) landed in #42 (merge 6930a43). M4 (tests and checks, building ADR 0001) and M5 (the review screen) are in progress on their branches. M6 is next, now that M3 is in."}},{"kind":"comment","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792677714,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"comment:6342661475"},"data":{"body":"## Handover: M4, tests and checks (branch b768fbb-m4-tests-and-checks)\n\nStep 4 now runs the tests and checks that the base branch's `.git-board.toml` declares (`[cycle.tests.\u003csuite\u003e]`, `[cycle.checks.\u003cname\u003e]`). Each run happens in a clean `git worktree add --detach` of the branch's last commit. Its result is a signed line in `refs/notes/ci/\u003cwriter\u003e` (ADR 0001). Mark ready for review is a server POST that refuses until every check is proven at the head. `git board verify` prints the same verdict from the command line. M1's test-file globs were renamed `[cycle] test-files`.\n\n### Checked\n\n- In a browser, on a clone of git-board-test in $TMPDIR (origin removed, so no live calls), at 1440 and 900px:\n  - a bug issue: the touched suite and check came pre-ticked;\n  - \"Run at \u003ctest commit\u003e\" gave FAIL, then the head gave PASS;\n  - Mark ready for review was refused, first with \"lint not run at …\", then with \"lint FAILED, signed by alice\";\n  - after the fix, lint passed and the issue moved to in-review;\n  - a feature issue showed the per-criterion rule and reused lint's PASS through the content key.\n- `git board verify` agrees with the page: proven at the head; exit 1 with the FAILED reason at the fix-with-TODO commit.\n- `make ci`: green except TestIssueSyncTakesTheAssigneesMode and TestForgeSyncSetsTheAssigneesMode, which fail on origin/main too. Its first run also caught TestAppendParallel leaking `ci-tmp` refs under load; the private ref now has no reflog and a longer packed-refs wait (bfbf51a), checked with 72 stressed runs. Web: typecheck is clean, 166/166 tests pass.\n\n### Changed beyond the plan\n\n- Files are matched by git glob pathspecs (`:(glob)`), not a new matcher.\n- The key carries a `dir` line.\n- The run POST takes `target: head|test`.\n- A `.pub` signingkey is accepted when its private key sits beside it.\n- The compare-and-swap retries until a deadline, not 10 times.\n- Tools are not in the key; they stay in the line.\n- The gate skips `where = \"ci\"` checks.\n- Propose skips sh/bash scripts. Its Makefile and package.json set is lint/vet/typecheck/type-check, and lefthook's `glob:` is not mapped.\n- verify computes the base with the git CLI, so a held git-bug lock doesn't stop it.\n- The browser check turned up four fixes, all in f3a84b6:\n  - step 4's wait is now worded by the kind's rule: \"write the tests\" for a feature, \"write the failing test\" for a bug;\n  - a card refusal no longer follows you to another step;\n  - the gate's time is local;\n  - an empty log reads \"(no output)\".\n\n### Left for later branches\n\n- Pushing and fetching `refs/notes/ci/*` with sync. The reader already takes the union of `refs/notes/remotes/*/ci/*`. The push command in docs/configuration.md was not run live, because pushes are denied in this sandbox.\n- The live-worktree feedback run; only the recorded run is built.\n- ssh-agent keys and literal `key::` signing keys are refused with a message.\n- `refs/notes/ci-tmp/*` refs left by a crash are not pruned.\n- A PATCH of the status (or a drag on the board) bypasses the gate; only the step's button is gated.\n- The land's sample re-run and the agents' deny rules belong to wtx. The run at the merged head is M6.\n- Once 0aa3715 lands: rebase, then Propose on git-board's own lefthook.yml.\n\n### Seen, not M4\n\n- TestIssueSyncTakesTheAssigneesMode and TestForgeSyncSetsTheAssigneesMode fail on origin/main too.\n- At 900px the header's Inbox overlaps Sync, and the \"Updated just now\" toast covers the bottom-left Run button.\n"}},{"kind":"comment","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792677714,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"comment:6342661770"},"data":{"body":"Rebased on main after M3 landed (6930a43); HEAD 7b65250.\n\n- Conflicts: worktrees.go (M3's approve action and planThen beside the review thread; the doc comment names both), board.ts (agentAction takes approve and comment), cycle.ts (step 3's draft suffix and step 6's review line). The overlap in prompt.go merged by itself: Then and Thread both stand.\n- make ci passes in full, the two assignees-mode tests included. The earlier failures were the sandbox: with main's new Go modules, make ci needs GOMODCACHE in TMPDIR there."}},{"kind":"comment","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792677715,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"comment:6342662089"},"data":{"body":"- **Gap, not built:** a status PATCH or a board drag into in-review is not gated. The PRD rules it so (\"Statuses are the stages\": the step follows the status, with a note when the evidence disagrees). Steps 5 and 6 do not yet show that note when the checks are not proven at the head. `GET /api/issues/{id}/tests` answers `gate.proven` and `gate.reason` for whoever builds it.\n- The two make ci failures (TestIssueSyncTakesTheAssigneesMode, TestForgeSyncSetsTheAssigneesMode) predate this branch: f463099 (#41) fixed them on main after its base 419779c. The land rebase brings the fix in."}},{"kind":"comment","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792677716,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"comment:6342662367"},"data":{"body":"The user approved, on 2026-10-22, the four answers to ADR 0001's \"Left open\" written in docs/configuration.md › Tests and checks:\n\n- the signers file is `.allowed_signers` (`[cycle] signers`), read at the base branch;\n- version commands (`tools`) and `env` are set per suite;\n- a clone's writer name comes from `git config git-board.writer`;\n- `git board verify` is the command-line verdict."}},{"kind":"comment","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792677717,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"comment:6342662601"},"data":{"body":"Rebased on origin/main after M4 landed (a573f14), with no conflicts; HEAD de2d189. make ci passes in full."}},{"kind":"comment","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792677718,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"comment:6342662927"},"data":{"body":"## M6 handover: steps 2 (Risk), 5 (Code), 7 (Verify)\n\nBranch `b768fbb-m6-risk-code-verify` at 6b94027, rebased on main 6a72039 (M4, PR #46). `make ci` passes at 6b94027.\n\n### What's in it\n- **Step 2 (C2), CycleRisk.vue:** the three classes in C2's words, the AI's suggestion, and Set \u003cclass\u003e. The server action `suggest-risk` (internal/ai: one OpenAI-compatible chat call) posts the AI's class as a step-2 comment (meta `ai:risk`, `ai:model`).\n- **Step 5 (C5), CycleCode.vue:** the agent strip, and the commits with a +/- total. The tiles show step 4's tests, the base's checks at the head (M4's gate, signed by whom), and the PR's checks. The PR's title and description can be edited; this adds ghpr `Edit` and `PATCH /api/issues/{id}/pulls/{n}`. Mark ready for review goes through M4's gated POST.\n- **Step 7 (C7), CycleVerify.vue:** who and when for each criterion (\"the merge\" when it was checked at the merge commit), the run tile, plan delivered, \"waits for k of n criteria\", and Sign off \u003cstatus\u003e / Send back.\n- **The run at the merged head, wired to M4:**\n  - `/tests` returns `merged`, which is `proof.Gate` at `pr.merge_commit`.\n  - The run tile reads Pass / Failed / Not run with the signer.\n  - When the base declares checks, the sign-off answers 400 \"not proven at \u003csha\u003e: \u003creason\u003e\", and a reason overrides it.\n  - Test: `TestCycleSignoffNotProvenAtMerge`.\n\n### Rulings\n- The AI's suggestion is a comment, never the risk field. A person sets the class.\n- The AI key comes only from `LLM_API_KEY` in the server's environment. When `LLM_BASE_URL`/`LLM_MODEL` are unset, the address and model fall back to the first provider in `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json`. opencode's auth store is never read. With no address, the AI is off and the box is hidden.\n- Board drags and status PATCHes skip the gates (the PRD's floor rule). Only the step's own button gates.\n- `Stages.Roles` was added, so step 2's footer and step 7's bar name the role.\n- Sign off stays disabled in the browser until every criterion is checked. The server keeps only the person rule and the run/proof rule.\n- When the base declares checks, the proof at the merge commit replaces a pasted run, and a reason overrides it. When no checks are declared, a pasted `verify:run` at the merge still counts, as before.\n- A merge commit that isn't fetched yet counts as not proven: `/tests` lists the declared checks as not proven, and the sign-off refuses without a reason. `proof.Gate` only errors when checks are declared.\n\n### Deferred\n- `[ai] model` in the toml (dev-cycle.md's M6), and a Settings › AI page.\n- A \"how\" line on a checked criterion, and per-commit +/- stats (the endpoint only has the total).\n- A server-side criteria gate on sign-off (today it's only in the browser).\n- An \"open the agent\" link from step 5's strip (the Worktrees tab covers it).\n- At 900px the header nav overlaps \"Send\"/\"Inbox\". That's existing nav code, not M6.\n\n### What was seen in the browser\n- Steps 2, 5 and 7 were checked at 1440px and 900px on a clone of guilbep/git-board-test in $TMPDIR.\n- The PR parts (draft PR #30, merged PR #31, the checks, the gate at head and merge) came from routed responses, because the sandbox clone has no git-bug GitHub token. The scratch PRs #30 and #31 and the branch m6-base are left on git-board-test.\n- No real AI call was made: no `LLM_API_KEY` in this session. The client is covered by httptest in internal/ai and by `TestCycleSuggestRisk*`.\n\n### Remaining\n- Nothing for M6. The coordinator rebases and lands."}},{"kind":"comment","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792679414,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"comment:6343272717"},"data":{"body":"M3 to M6 have all landed: #42 (M3), #46 (M4), #47 (M5) and #48 (M6). The Approve `--build` follow-up landed too, with wtx 631df3f (`wtx brief --build`). Each landed with `make ci` green.\n\nOn guilbep/git-board-test the live run passed M3's Done-when:\n- Start opened a worktree, and the plan went into draft PR #32;\n- Approve continued the agent's own conversation in auto mode;\n- once the PR was marked ready, Mark ready for review moved the issue to in-review and Review unlocked.\n\nThe scratch PRs and branches are deleted.\n\nThe deferred items and the live-run findings are in 8c9b8ac (ready, p2). Closing."}}]}